WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.783
"Now what?" Zann said.

2
00:00:02.784 --> 00:00:08.367
He and his friends were huddled beneath some trees, hidden from the dragons flying overhead.

3
00:00:08.368 --> 00:00:15.813
"This is bad," Perda said. "We're lost, and we don't have any way to contact Arrano and the others."

4
00:00:15.814 --> 00:00:20.452
Just then a loud squawk came from directly above them.

5
00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:25.181
"It's the dragons!" Gliss cried. "They found us!"

6
00:00:25.182 --> 00:00:31.507
"No, wait." Darb peered up at the branches. "That didn't sound like a dragon."

7
00:00:31.508 --> 00:00:36.560
Zann looked up too. A large bird was perched on an upper branch.

8
00:00:36.561 --> 00:00:40.506
"That looks a lot like Teplo's sniffer goose," Darb said.

9
00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:43.523
"Only smaller and with a shorter neck."

10
00:00:43.524 --> 00:00:49.377
Perda sighed. "This is no time for identifying native species, Darb.

11
00:00:49.378 --> 00:00:52.659
Besides, that goose doesn't look very friendly.

12
00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:58.365
Let’s get moving." She grabbed Darb's arm and started to drag him away.

13
00:00:58.366 --> 00:01:03.219
"Quiet!" Gliss warned. "Here comes a dragon."

14
00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:07.966
Zann hid behind a tree as a medium-sized dragon walked past.

15
00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:13.043
With every step thick orange smoke puffed out of its nostrils.

16
00:01:13.044 --> 00:01:17.582
"This is crazy," Zann said once the dragon was out of sight.

17
00:01:17.583 --> 00:01:21.719
"We can't just wander around looking for that wormhole."

18
00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:29.332
"Yeah," Perda agreed. "Besides, we'll have to use magic to levitate over the boiling lake anyway.

19
00:01:29.333 --> 00:01:32.494
Let's just save time and zap there."

20
00:01:32.495 --> 00:01:36.894
"We can't," Gliss said. "We're lost, remember?"

21
00:01:36.895 --> 00:01:40.348
"I can try a Seeking spell," Perda offered.

22
00:01:40.349 --> 00:01:44.222
"That's how I found the wormhole back in Swamp Bottom."

23
00:01:44.223 --> 00:01:47.867
"Good idea," Zann said. "Join friction."

24
00:01:47.868 --> 00:01:54.258
Perda, Gliss, and Zann rubbed their hands together. "Seek," Perda said.

25
00:01:54.259 --> 00:01:59.085
"It's working!" Zann could feel the magic energy tugging at him.

26
00:01:59.086 --> 00:02:03.154
The Seeking spell led them through the valley below the trees.

27
00:02:03.155 --> 00:02:08.972
Zann was climbing over some large rocks when he heard a rustling sound overhead.

28
00:02:08.973 --> 00:02:13.268
He looked up and saw a large dragon flying straight at them.

29
00:02:13.269 --> 00:02:17.143
"Everyone get down!" he shouted.Zann

30
00:02:17.144 --> 00:02:24.822
threw himself behind a boulder. A blast of fiery air hit the spot where he'd just been standing. "I

31
00:02:24.823 --> 00:02:27.622
think that's a flame fury!" Darb said. "Like

32
00:02:27.623 --> 00:02:32.664
the ones that powered the Dragon Wagon. They must come from this world!" "Great,"

33
00:02:32.665 --> 00:02:38.463
Gliss said grimly. "All the more reason to get out of here!" "We'd

34
00:02:38.464 --> 00:02:42.323
better zap away," Zann said. "Zap!" He

35
00:02:42.324 --> 00:02:45.081
felt a twinge, but nothing happened. "Oh

36
00:02:45.082 --> 00:02:50.978
no!" Perda cried. "That Seeking spell used up our magic energy!" The

37
00:02:50.979 --> 00:02:53.682
fury was circling toward them again. Flames

38
00:02:53.683 --> 00:02:58.281
were already curling out of its snout. Darb stood up. "Darb!"

39
00:02:58.282 --> 00:03:02.411
Gliss cried. "Get down!" Cupping

40
00:03:02.412 --> 00:03:09.462
both hands around his mouth, Darb took a deep breath and let out a loud honking sound. "What

41
00:03:09.463 --> 00:03:11.690
are you—" Zann began. Suddenly

42
00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:16.217
an answering honk came from the direction of the trees! A

43
00:03:16.218 --> 00:03:22.844
second later the goose flapped into sight and spit a blob of goo directly at the dragon. The

44
00:03:22.845 --> 00:03:27.322
fury howled, falling to the ground with an earth-shaking thump. It

45
00:03:27.323 --> 00:03:32.794
pawed frantically at its face, trying to rub away the thick goose spit. "What

46
00:03:32.795 --> 00:03:37.184
are we waiting for?" Perda cried. "Run!" Zann

47
00:03:37.185 --> 00:03:41.841
took off with the girls at his heels and Zing flying overhead. Darb

48
00:03:41.842 --> 00:03:46.905
paused just long enough to give a honk of thanks and then followed. They'd

49
00:03:46.906 --> 00:03:52.341
only been running for a few minutes when they almost stumbled over a wormhole. "The

50
00:03:52.342 --> 00:03:56.951
Seeking spell found a different wormhole!" Gliss exclaimed. "Good,"

51
00:03:56.952 --> 00:04:02.978
Perda said, panting. "We might not have enough energy left to levitate. And

52
00:04:02.979 --> 00:04:07.127
I definitely didn't feel like swimming in that lake again!" Darb

53
00:04:07.128 --> 00:04:10.479
cast a nervous glance over his shoulder. "I

54
00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:14.360
think I hear that dragon coming. Hurry!" Zann

55
00:04:14.361 --> 00:04:26.309
grabbed Perda's hand. Perda held out her hand to Gliss, who was holding Darb's hand. They all dived into the wormhole. Soon

56
00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:29.873
the friends were hurtling through the vortex. "Hold

57
00:04:29.874 --> 00:04:37.472
tight, everyone," Gliss said. "It makes me nervous to be here without our Shackle spell." "Hey,

58
00:04:37.473 --> 00:04:42.674
Darb," said Zann. "How did you know that goose would help us?" "I

59
00:04:42.675 --> 00:04:47.470
remembered the fake snuffer goose from the Dragon Wagon," Darb explained. "When

60
00:04:47.471 --> 00:04:53.569
I realized we were in the furies' home world, I guessed that goose we saw must have been a snuffer." "But

61
00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:57.335
how did you know how to call it?" Perda asked. "Because

62
00:04:57.336 --> 00:05:01.227
of Teplo’s pet sniffer goose," Darb said. "I

63
00:05:01.228 --> 00:05:05.923
picked up a few words of its language while we were staying with Teplo. Since

64
00:05:05.924 --> 00:05:14.969
sniffer and snuffer geese look similar, I guessed their languages might be related." He shrugged. "Luckily, I was right." "Wow."

65
00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:19.736
Zann was impressed. He never would have thought of any of that! "You

66
00:05:19.737 --> 00:05:22.686
saved us from being roasted, Darb." "Yeah."

67
00:05:22.687 --> 00:05:28.080
Gliss shuddered. "Roasted and eaten ."

68
00:05:28.081 --> 00:05:32.818
"Hey, Zann," Perda said. "Your purple marks are glowing again."

69
00:05:32.819 --> 00:05:36.223
Zann grabbed at the next wormhole and tumbled through it.

70
00:05:36.224 --> 00:05:41.672
Jumping to his feet, he was prepared to fight or run, but he quickly relaxed.

71
00:05:41.673 --> 00:05:44.549
This world didn't look scary at all.

72
00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:48.591
"Where are we?" Gliss wondered, climbing to her feet.

73
00:05:48.592 --> 00:05:53.087
Perda shrugged. "Wherever it is, it looks boring."

74
00:05:53.088 --> 00:06:01.284
"Yeah." Zann stepped away from the wormhole, which swirled shut and disappeared, leaving almost no color anywhere.

75
00:06:01.285 --> 00:06:09.263
Everything—the sky, the ground, the trees and shrubs—was dull shades of beige and gray.

76
00:06:09.264 --> 00:06:14.065
"At least there aren't any scary creatures attacking us," Gliss said.

77
00:06:14.066 --> 00:06:21.481
Darb nodded. "I don't see any signs of people either. How are we going to figure out if Wyssa's here?"

78
00:06:21.482 --> 00:06:26.902
"Zing!" Perda scolded. "Don't eat that. We don't know if it's safe."

79
00:06:26.903 --> 00:06:31.884
The dragon was nibbling on a leaf. "He must be hungry," Zann said.

80
00:06:31.885 --> 00:06:36.653
"I am too. Let's conjure some food while we figure out what to do."

81
00:06:36.654 --> 00:06:45.204
"I'll do it." Gliss rubbed her hands together, but nothing happened. She frowned. "It's not working."

82
00:06:45.205 --> 00:06:54.679
"Uh-oh." Zann gulped. "What if we're stuck in another world without magic?"

